hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20598","In the year two hundred and twenty-eight, Waki' narrated to us, Mis'ar ibn Habib al-Jarmi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Salamah narrated to me, from his father, that they came as a delegation to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; when they wanted to leave, they said: O Messenger of Allah, who will lead us? He said: The one of you who has gathered most Qur'an, or taken most Qur'an. He said: No one of the people had gathered of the Qur'an what I had gathered. He said: So they put me forward while I was a boy, and I used to lead them, with a wrapper on me. He said: I never witnessed a gathering of Jarm except that I was their imam, and I pray over their funerals to this day of mine."
"20599","Isma'il informed us, Ayyub informed us, from 'Amr ibn Salamah, he said: We were at a settlement, and riders - Isma'il once said: People - would pass by us returning from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so I would draw near them and listen until I memorized Qur'an; and the people were waiting with their Islam for the conquest of Makkah; when it was conquered, a man would come to him saying: O Messenger of Allah, I am the delegate of Banu so-and-so, and I have come to you with their Islam; so my father set out with his people's Islam, and returned to them, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Put forward the one of you with most Qur'an. He said: They looked, while I was upon a great cushion, and found no one among them with more Qur'an than me, so they put me forward while I was a boy, and I prayed with them, wearing a cloak; when I bowed or prostrated it would shrink, exposing my private parts; when we prayed, an old woman among us, aged, said: Cover from us the backside of your reciter. So they cut a shirt for me, and he mentioned that he rejoiced in it greatly."
"20600","'Ali ibn 'Asim said: Khalid al-Hadhdha' informed me, from Abu Qilabah, from 'Amr ibn Salamah, he said: Riders used to come to us from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we would learn Qur'an from them, and they would narrate that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let the one with most Qur'an among you lead you."
